      "writtenOn": "2024-11-12T16:00:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this is a relatively minor issue, because these fragments get included in the actual .bp file, so they will be findable and highlighted in that context.\n\nI\u0027m not familiar with bpfmt, but my guess is that modifying it could be weird and hackish, because it\u0027s not really specified what a \"fragment\" even is. Some are snippets to include inside rules, some are full rules that get included at the top level.\n\nAnd since there are relatively few of them, I think it\u0027s a worthwhile tradeoff to be able to turn on the bpfmt preupload check, which was my motivation for this set of changes.\n\nI feel like the *best* solution is to get rid of the *.bp.fragment files entirely. I was able to do this for the fragments that were merely specifying visibility, but it\u0027s probably not feasible in general.",
      "parentUuid": "82a9111e_8c44d49b",
      "revId": "d4d3ecf934d4aaf44cd082a5210253b96ce17d36",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
